alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure doc "The css_rules_oracle entry, invoked as `css_rules_oracle PATH` with PATH naming the case file that tests/css/rules_oracle.py writes, relative to the working directory: per case, a line holding the suite index and the byte length in decimal separated by one space, the bytes and a line feed. The suite indexes are 0 stylesheet, 1 rule_list, 2 declaration_list, 3 blocks_contents, 4 one_rule and 5 one_declaration. For every case it runs parse_component_values, then the suite's pkg::css::rules function over the whole component list, and prints one line: the result as JSON in css-parsing-tests' representation, an array of items for a list suite and one item or its error for a one suite, each range as the array of the component values it names with numbers as pkg::oracle::css_json writes them. A range that is not a run of siblings of the list prints as the JSON string `\"driver: invalid range S..E in item N\"`, a name span outside the list's text as `\"driver: invalid name span in item N\"`, and a malformed component inside a range as pkg::oracle::css_json's fault string. A case that parse_component_values refuses prints as `\"driver: tokenizer refused\"`, and one that a list function refuses as `\"driver: rules refused\"`. It exits with 0 after printing every case, and with 2, after the cases before it, when the case file cannot be read or is malformed, including a suite index past 5.";
